       "data": "Out[478]= \\begin{matrix}\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{rows used ((i1,j1), (i2,j2))} & \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 1\\\\2 & 1\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{norms with det != 0} & 12\\text{ / }12\\\\\\hline\\text{cross pairs with det = 0} & 42\\text{ / }42\\\\\\hline\\text{cross pairs with N.($\\Delta$tc1, $\\Delta$c) = 0} & 42\\text{ / }42\\\\\\hline\\text{cross pairs with N = 0 identically} & \\begin{pmatrix}\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,4,0,0\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,2,2,2\\right\\}\\\\\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,3,1,0\\right\\} & \\left\\{3,2,2,1\\right\\}\\\\\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,2,2,0\\right\\} & \\left\\{3,3,1,1\\right\\}\\\\\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{3,3,1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,2,2,0\\right\\}\\\\\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{3,2,2,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,3,1,0\\right\\}\\\\\\left\\{2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,2,2,2\\right\\} & \\left\\{4,4,0,0\\right\\}\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}\\\\\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{(S,P)} & \\text{mu\\_A} & \\text{mu\\_B} & \\text{kind} & \\text{det N} & \\text{N.$\\Delta$ = 0} & \\text{rank N}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,2,0,0\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,2,0,0\\right\\} & \\text{norm} & -\\frac{520}{21} & \\mathrm{True} & 2\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,2,0,0\\right\\} & \\left\\{2,1,1,0\\right\\} & \\text{cross} & 0 & \\mat… [latex truncated: 7363 chars total]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "63661a10-dae2-4795-aa64-f2dafe4b2f10"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Results\n\n- **Q-functions (cell 4).** All 12 irreps of `(1,1)`, `(2,1)`, `(2,2)`: unique gauge-fixed solutions; `O q_k^{[2]} = 0` and `O† q^j = 0` identically in `u`.\n- **Integrals of motion (cell 6).** The Casimir-form `tc` equal the Baxter-solved `tc` for all 12 irreps, and the three identities `ΔT_1 = Δtc_1`, `ΔT_2 = ¼Δtc_1(τ_1^{vac}+τ_1^{vac[-2]}) + Δc`, `ΔT_3 = ν_4ν_1^{[-4]}Δtc_1` hold symbolically. Of the eight twisted differences only `Δtc_1 = (h^2/2)ΔC_2` and `Δc` remain independent.\n- **Per-ladder rows, one `(i,j)` (cells 9-11).** `det N^{AA} ≠ 0` for every irrep exactly for `(2,1), (2,2), (3,1), (3,2), (3,3), (4,1), (4,2), (4,3)`; zero for every irrep otherwise, including the four twisted pairings `i ∈ {1,2}, j ∈ {3,4}`. At `(2,1)`: norms nonzero 12/12; cross determinants zero 42/42; `N·(Δtc_1, Δc) = 0` for 42/42.\n- **Full-contour rows, a different `(i,j)` per row (cells 13-14).** A full-contour row vanishes identically for every irrep exactly when `i < j`. The other ten rows fall into proportionality classes, `(1,1) ∝ (4,4)` and `(2,2) ∝ (3,2) ∝ (3,3)`, and a pair of rows from one class gives a vanishing norm. The remaining 41 of the 120 pairs of rows give `det Ñ^{AA} ≠ 0` for all 12 irreps; no pair works for only some irreps. At rows `((1,1), (2,1))`: norms nonzero 12/12; cross determinants zero 42/42; `Ñ·(Δtc_1, Δc) = 0` for 42/42.\n- **Open.** For 6 ordered cross pairs at `(2,2)` — `{4,4,0,0}↔{2,2,2,2}`, `{4,3,1,0}↔{3,2,2,1}`, `{4,2,2,0}↔{3,3,1,1}` — every row vanishes: all 16 full-contour rows and all 32 per-ladder rows, for every `(i,j)`. So the matrix is identically zero for any choice, and orthogonality there is not tested by this system. The vanishing is therefore structural, not an artefact of the choice of Q-functions. Descendants share `tc` with their highest weight and are not separated at zero twist.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5. Relation to the honest Hilbert-space norm\n\nAt zero twist, the transfer matrices are $\\mathfrak{gl}(4)$-invariant, so one transfer-matrix eigenvalue labels a whole multiplet. The Baxter $Q$-functions above label the highest-weight line of each multiplicity-one irrep. We therefore restrict the transfer matrices to the total-weight sector equal to the irrep's highest weight $\\mu$; the required eigenline is one-dimensional there after its eigenvalue is imposed.\n\nFor every state we construct a right vector from\n$$\n(\\tau_a-\\tau_a^{(A)}\\,\\mathbf 1)\\Psi_R=0\n$$\nand a left vector as a right eigenvector of the transpose,\n$$\n(\\tau_a^{\\mathsf T}-\\tau_a^{(A)}\\,\\mathbf 1)\\Psi_L=0.\n$$\nOnly $\\tau_1,\\tau_2$ need to be checked because they are the two independent zero-twist transfer-matrix directions at $L=2$; $\\tau_3$ is dependent as proved above.\n\nBoth eigenvectors have an independent scaling freedom. To make the comparison reproducible, each is put in **pivot gauge**: its first nonzero component in the ordered tensor-product GT basis is set to one. The honest bilinear norm in this gauge is\n$$\n\\mathcal H_A=\\Psi_L\\cdot\\Psi_R.\n$$\nThe SoV determinant is then related by the exact, gauge-dependent conversion factor\n$$\n\\det N^{AA}=C_A\\,\\mathcal H_A,\\qquad C_A=\\frac{\\det N^{AA}}{\\Psi_L\\cdot\\Psi_R}.\n$$",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 10. Exact GT-basis transfer matrices, self-contained for the honest-norm comparison. ---- *)\nClearAll[hnPs, hnDim, hnJ0, hnJp, hnJm, hnJJ, hnV, hnH, hnLax, hnTmono, hnTg, hnQminV, hnTauV];\nhnPs[rep_] := hnPs[rep] = Block[\n   {res = Prepend[rep, #] & /@ Tuples[Table[Range[rep[[1, i + 1]], rep[[1, i]]], {i, 1, Length[rep[[1]]] - 1}]]},\n   If[Length[res[[1, 1]]] == 1, Reverse@Sort@res, Reverse@Sort@Flatten[hnPs /@ res, 1]]\n   ];\nhnDim[rep_] := hnDim[rep] = Length[hnPs[{rep}]];\nhnJ0[k_][pat_] := hnJ0[k][pat] = Sum[pat[[k, i]], {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat[[k - 1, i]], {i, 1, k - 1}];\nhnJp[k_][pat_] := hnJp[k][pat] = -Sum[\n    Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k + 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]/\n     Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}]\n     hnV[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] + 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nhnJm[k_][pat_] := hnJm[k][pat] = Sum[\n    Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k - 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]/\n     Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}]\n     hnV[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] - 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nhnJJ[k_, l_, rep_] := hnJJ[k, l, rep] = Which[\n   k == l, DiagonalMatrix[hnJ0[k] /@ hnPs[{rep}]],\n   l == k + 1, Transpose@Table[Coefficient[hnJp[k][hnPs[{rep}][[i]]], hnV[#]] & /@ hnPs[{rep}], {i, hnDim[rep]}],\n   l == k - 1, Transpose@Table[Coefficient[hnJm[l][hnPs[{rep}][[i]]], hnV[#]] & /@ hnPs[{rep}], {i, hnDim[rep]}],\n   l > k + 1, hnJJ[k, k + 1, rep] . hnJJ[k + 1, l, rep] - hnJJ[k + 1, l, rep] . hnJJ[k, k + 1, rep],\n   l < k - 1, hnJJ[k, k - 1, rep] . hnJJ[k - 1, l, rep] - hnJJ[k - 1, l, rep] . hnJJ[k, k - 1, rep]\n   ];\nhnH = 1;\nhnLax[lam_, x_] := hnLax[lam, x] = Table[\n   SparseArray[x KroneckerDelta[i, j] IdentityMatrix[hnDim[lam]] - hnH hnJJ[j, i, lam]], {i, 4}, {j, 4}];\nhnTmono[sites_, x_] := hnTmono[sites, x] = Fold[\n   Function[{mon, site}, With[{lx = hnLax[site[[1]], x - site[[2]]]},\n     Table[Sum[KroneckerProduct[mon[[i, k]], lx[[k, j]]], {k, 4}], {i, 4}, {j, 4}]]],\n   hnLax[sites[[1, 1]], x - sites[[1, 2]]], Rest[sites]];\nhnTg[sites_, zs_, x_][i_, j_] := zs[[i]] hnTmono[sites, x][[i, j]];\nhnQminV[sites_, zs_, inds_List, x_, vec_] := Sum[\n   Module[{res = vec},\n    Do[res = hnTg[sites, zs, x - (k - 1) hnH][inds[[perm[[k]]]], inds[[k]]] . res,\n     {k, Length[inds], 1, -1}];\n    Signature[perm] res], {perm, Permutations[Range[Length[inds]]]}];\nhnTauV[sites_, zs_, a_, x_, vec_] := Sum[hnQminV[sites, zs, inds, x, vec], {inds, Subsets[Range[4], {a}]}];\nGrid[{{\"status\", \"exact GT generators and transfer matrices loaded\"}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"969947\" data-output-id=\"2\" data-out-n=\"37\" data-sub-idx=\"14\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"18\" data-sub-start=\"37\" data-sub-end=\"37\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[37]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"10\" data-latex-b64=\"XGJlZ2lue2FycmF5fXt8Y3xjfH1caGxpbmVcdGV4dHtzdGF0dXN9ICYgXHRleHR7ZXhhY3QgR1QgZ2VuZXJhdG9ycyBhbmQgdHJhbnNmZXIgbWF0cmljZXMgbG9hZGVkfVxcXGhsaW5lXGVuZHthcnJheX0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.24em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.89em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:1.2em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.85em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">status</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:1.2em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.85em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">exact GT generators and transfer matrices loaded</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:1.2em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.35em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.65em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.85em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.35em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
