   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "The table gives the exact conversion factors for all 12 benchmark irreps. Every right and transpose-left vector satisfies both independent transfer-matrix eigenvalue equations exactly.\n\nThe equality is therefore established in the chosen gauges as\n$$\n\\boxed{\\det N^{AA}=C_A\\,\\Psi_L\\cdot\\Psi_R.}\n$$\nThe factors $C_A$ vary with the irrep. This variation is expected: monic/gauge-fixed Baxter polynomials and pivot-normalized Hilbert-space eigenvectors are two different state normalizations. Without specifying both eigenvector scales, $\\Psi_L\\cdot\\Psi_R$ itself is not invariant, since $\\Psi_R\\to a\\Psi_R$ and $\\Psi_L\\to b\\Psi_L$ multiply it by $ab$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 5.1 Vacuum-normalized SoV norm\n\nFor fixed $(S,P)$, define the vacuum state by\n$$\n\\mu_{\\mathrm{vac}}=\\{S+P,S+P,0,0\\},\n$$\nand use its diagonal determinant as the common denominator,\n$$\nN^{\\mathrm{vac}}_{S,P}=\\det N^{\\mathrm{vac},\\mathrm{vac}}.\n$$\nThe normalized SoV norm is\n$$\n\\widehat N^A_{S,P}=\\frac{\\det N^{AA}}{N^{\\mathrm{vac}}_{S,P}}.\n$$\nThe default functions below use the good per-ladder pairing $(i,j)=(2,1)$. Optional pairing arguments keep the definition reusable for the other good pairings.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 12. Vacuum-normalized diagonal SoV norms. Default good pairing: (i,j) = (2,1). ---- *)\nClearAll[vacuumState, NAA, Nvac, Nnormalized, normalizedNormData];\nvacuumState[S_, P_] := First@Select[\n   states[S, P], #[\"mu\"] === {S + P, S + P, 0, 0} &];\n\nNAA[S_, P_, state_, i_: 2, j_: 1] := Together@Det@N2d[S, P, state, state, i, j];\nNvac[S_, P_, i_: 2, j_: 1] := Nvac[S, P, i, j] =\n   NAA[S, P, vacuumState[S, P], i, j];\nNnormalized[S_, P_, state_, i_: 2, j_: 1] :=\n   Together[NAA[S, P, state, i, j]/Nvac[S, P, i, j]];\n\nnormalizedNormData = Map[\n   Function[row, With[\n     {sp = row[\"SP\"], state = First@Select[states @@ row[\"SP\"], #[\"mu\"] === row[\"mu\"] &]},\n     Join[row, <|\n       \"Nvac\" -> Nvac @@ sp,\n       \"normalizedSoVNorm\" -> Nnormalized[sp[[1]], sp[[2]], state]\n       |>]\n     ]],\n   honestNormData];\n\nGrid[{\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[\n     ({#, Nvac @@ #} &) /@ {{1, 1}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}},\n     {\"(S,P)\", \"Nvac\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]},\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[\n     ({#[\"SP\"], #[\"mu\"], #[\"SoVNorm\"], #[\"Nvac\"], #[\"normalizedSoVNorm\"]} &) /@\n      normalizedNormData,\n     {\"(S,P)\", \"mu\", \"det N\", \"Nvac\", \"normalized det N\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]},\n  {Grid[{{\"all vacuum-normalized norms equal 1\",\n      And @@ Table[\n        Nnormalized[sp[[1]], sp[[2]], vacuumState @@ sp] === 1,\n        {sp, {{1, 1}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}}}]}},\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}\n  }, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
