   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "By construction the vacuum row equals one for every $(S,P)$. In terms of the honest bilinear norm,\n$$\n\\widehat N^A_{S,P}\n =\\frac{C_A}{C_{\\mathrm{vac}}}\n  \\frac{\\Psi_L^A\\cdot\\Psi_R^A}\n       {\\Psi_L^{\\mathrm{vac}}\\cdot\\Psi_R^{\\mathrm{vac}}}.\n$$\nIn the pivot gauge used above, the vacuum honest norm is one in all three benchmark chains.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 5.2 All nonzero per-ladder pairings\n\nThe allowed pairings are\n$$\n(i,j)\\in\\{(2,1),(2,2),(3,1),(3,2),(3,3),(4,1),(4,2),(4,3)\\},\n$$\nwhere $i$ labels the direct $q_i$ and $j$ labels the dual $q^j$. Each pairing has its own raw determinant and therefore its own vacuum denominator:\n$$\n\\widehat N^{A}_{i,j;S,P}\n =\\frac{\\det N^{AA}_{i,j;S,P}}\n        {\\det N^{\\mathrm{vac},\\mathrm{vac}}_{i,j;S,P}}.\n$$\nPairings with zero vacuum determinant are excluded because this ratio is undefined. In particular, no pairing involving $q^4$ is allowed, while the lowest-dual-degree viable choices are $(3,3)$ and $(4,3)$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 13. Raw and vacuum-normalized norms for every allowed nonzero pairing. ---- *)\nClearAll[allowedPairings, benchmarkSP, pairingNormData, pairingSummary, pairingComparisonData];\nallowedPairings = {{2, 1}, {2, 2}, {3, 1}, {3, 2}, {3, 3}, {4, 1}, {4, 2}, {4, 3}};\nbenchmarkSP = {{1, 1}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}};\n\npairingNormData = Flatten[\n   Table[\n    With[{i = pair[[1]], j = pair[[2]], S = sp[[1]], P = sp[[2]]},\n     Table[With[\n       {raw = NAA[S, P, state, i, j], vac = Nvac[S, P, i, j]},\n       <|\"pairing\" -> pair, \"SP\" -> sp, \"mu\" -> state[\"mu\"],\n        \"NAA\" -> raw, \"Nvac\" -> vac, \"normalizedNorm\" -> Together[raw/vac]|>\n       ], {state, states[S, P]}]\n     ],\n    {pair, allowedPairings}, {sp, benchmarkSP}], 3];\n\npairingSummary = Table[\n   With[{rows = Select[pairingNormData, #[\"pairing\"] === pair &]},\n    {pair,\n     Count[rows, row_ /; row[\"NAA\"] =!= 0],\n     Table[First@Cases[rows,\n        row_ /; row[\"SP\"] === sp && row[\"mu\"] === {Total[sp], Total[sp], 0, 0} :> row[\"Nvac\"]],\n      {sp, benchmarkSP}],\n     And @@ Cases[rows,\n       row_ /; row[\"mu\"] === {Total[row[\"SP\"]], Total[row[\"SP\"]], 0, 0} :>\n        (row[\"normalizedNorm\"] === 1)]\n     }], {pair, allowedPairings}];\n\npairingComparisonData = Flatten[\n   Table[\n    Table[With[\n      {values = Table[\n         Nnormalized[sp[[1]], sp[[2]], state, pair[[1]], pair[[2]]],\n         {pair, allowedPairings}]},\n      {sp, state[\"mu\"], SameQ @@ values, Length@DeleteDuplicates[values]}\n      ], {state, states @@ sp}],\n    {sp, benchmarkSP}], 1];\n\nGrid[{\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[pairingSummary,\n     {\"(i,j)\", \"nonzero diagonal norms, of 12\",\n      \"Nvac for (1,1), (2,1), (2,2)\", \"all three vacuum ratios = 1\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]},\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[pairingComparisonData,\n     {\"(S,P)\", \"mu\", \"same normalized norm for all 8 pairings\",\n      \"number of distinct normalized values\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]},\n  {Grid[{\n     {\"allowed list agrees with the exhaustive survey\",\n      allowedPairings === Cases[normSurvey, {pair_, 3, 3, 6} :> pair]},\n     {\"all allowed diagonal norms nonzero\", Count[pairingNormData, row_ /; row[\"NAA\"] =!= 0] === 96},\n     {\"stored pairing/state records\", Length[pairingNormData]}\n     }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}\n  }, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
