   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "The complete 8 x 12 = 96 ledger is stored in pairingNormData. Each record contains the pairing, (S,P), irrep, raw determinant, pairing-specific vacuum determinant, and normalized norm.\n\nVacuum normalization does **not** remove the Q-pairing dependence at the benchmark point. Only the three vacuum states agree across all pairings, trivially because each is normalized to one. Every one of the nine non-vacuum irreps has eight distinct normalized values, one for each allowed pairing. Thus a specific pairing—or a further pairing-dependent conversion to Hilbert-space normalization—must remain part of the norm convention.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 5.3 First residue-pair contribution, with symbolic Q-functions\n\nWrite $\\mathcal Q(u)=q_A^{\\,j}(u)$, $Q(u)=q_i^A(u)$, and\n$$\n\\Delta Q(u)=Q(u)-Q(u-h).\n$$\nFor generic non-colliding ladders the measure factorizes as\n$$\nE_2(u)=\n\\frac{1}{\n \\prod_{k=0}^{S+1}(u-\\theta_1-kh)\n \\prod_{\\ell=0}^{P+1}(u-\\theta_2-\\ell h)}.\n$$\nLet $r_{1,k}$ and $r_{2,\\ell}$ be the two-component residue rows at $u=\\theta_1+kh$ and $u=\\theta_2+\\ell h$. Then\n$$\nN^{AA}_{i,j}=\n\\begin{pmatrix}\n\\sum_{k=0}^{S+1}r_{1,k}\\\\\n\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{P+1}r_{2,\\ell}\n\\end{pmatrix},\n\\qquad\n\\det N^{AA}_{i,j}\n=\\sum_{k=0}^{S+1}\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{P+1}\n \\det\\!\\begin{pmatrix}r_{1,k}\\\\r_{2,\\ell}\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\nThus the literal first term is the $k=\\ell=0$ residue pair.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 14. Symbolic k=l=0 residue-pair contribution to det N, no state inserted. ---- *)\nClearAll[qDualSymbolic, qDirectSymbolic, deltaQSymbolic, sSpin, pSpin,\n firstResidueWeight1, firstResidueWeight2, firstResidueRow1, firstResidueRow2,\n firstPositiveProduct, firstNegativeProduct, firstResidueDet, firstResidueDetClosed];\n\ndeltaQSymbolic[x_] := qDirectSymbolic[x] - qDirectSymbolic[x - h];\n\nfirstResidueWeight1 =\n (-1)^(sSpin + 1)/\n  (h^(sSpin + 1) Factorial[sSpin + 1]\n   Product[θ1 - θ2 - k h, {k, 0, pSpin + 1}]);\n\nfirstResidueWeight2 =\n (-1)^(pSpin + 1)/\n  (h^(pSpin + 1) Factorial[pSpin + 1]\n   Product[θ2 - θ1 - k h, {k, 0, sSpin + 1}]);\n\n(* At u=theta_s, nu4 vanishes. These are the complete two-component residues. *)\nfirstResidueRow1 = firstResidueWeight1 qDualSymbolic[θ1] {\n   (sSpin + 1) h (θ1 - θ2 - (pSpin + 1) h) deltaQSymbolic[θ1],\n   qDirectSymbolic[θ1 - h]\n   };\n\nfirstResidueRow2 = firstResidueWeight2 qDualSymbolic[θ2] {\n   -(pSpin + 1) h (θ1 - θ2 + (sSpin + 1) h) deltaQSymbolic[θ2],\n   qDirectSymbolic[θ2 - h]\n   };\n\nfirstPositiveProduct = Together[firstResidueRow1[[1]] firstResidueRow2[[2]]];\nfirstNegativeProduct = Together[firstResidueRow1[[2]] firstResidueRow2[[1]]];\nfirstResidueDet = Together[firstPositiveProduct - firstNegativeProduct];\n\nfirstResidueDetClosed = Together[\n firstResidueWeight1 firstResidueWeight2\n qDualSymbolic[θ1] qDualSymbolic[θ2] h (\n   (sSpin + 1) (θ1 - θ2 - (pSpin + 1) h)\n    deltaQSymbolic[θ1] qDirectSymbolic[θ2 - h]\n   + (pSpin + 1) (θ1 - θ2 + (sSpin + 1) h)\n    qDirectSymbolic[θ1 - h] deltaQSymbolic[θ2])\n ];\n\nGrid[{\n  {\"first pole on ladder 1\", θ1},\n  {\"first pole on ladder 2\", θ2},\n  {\"measure residue at theta1\", firstResidueWeight1},\n  {\"measure residue at theta2\", firstResidueWeight2},\n  {\"r_(1,0)\", firstResidueRow1},\n  {\"r_(2,0)\", firstResidueRow2},\n  {\"first positive determinant product\", firstPositiveProduct},\n  {\"first negative determinant product\", firstNegativeProduct},\n  {\"first residue-pair term D_(0,0)\", firstResidueDetClosed},\n  {\"direct Det[{r_(1,0),r_(2,0)}] agrees\", Together[firstResidueDet - firstResidueDetClosed] === 0}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
