   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Write\n\n$$\nH_A=\\Psi_L^A\\!\\cdot\\!\\Psi_R^A,\n\\qquad\nC_{A;i,j}=\\frac{N^{AA}_{i,j}}{H_A}.\n$$\n\nThen the exact relation is\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\n\\mathcal N^{(00)}_{A;i,j}\n=\\Gamma_{A;i,j}\\,\\frac{H_A}{H_{\\rm vac}},\n\\qquad\n\\Gamma_{A;i,j}\n=\\frac{C_{A;i,j}}{C_{{\\rm vac};i,j}}\n \\frac{D^{{\\rm vac}}_{00;i,j}}{D^{A}_{00;i,j}}\n}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\frac{H_A}{H_{\\rm vac}}\n=\\frac{\\mathcal N^{(00)}_{A;i,j}}{\\Gamma_{A;i,j}}.\n$$\n\nAt the benchmark point, all 24 vacuum checks give $\\mathcal N^{(00)}_{\\rm vac}=1$, and all 96 records verify the boxed identity exactly. However, $\\Gamma=1$ only for the three vacuum records within each pairing. Each non-vacuum state has eight distinct values of both $\\mathcal N^{(00)}$ and $\\Gamma$ over the eight allowed pairings. Thus dividing by $D_{00}$ and then by its vacuum value fixes the vacuum normalization, but it does **not** by itself convert the SoV determinant into the honest eigenvector norm.\n\nWith the present pivot normalization of the transfer-matrix eigenvectors, $H_{\\rm vac}=1$. Hence here $H_A=\\mathcal N^{(00)}_{A;i,j}/\\Gamma_{A;i,j}$. The remaining problem is to determine $\\Gamma_{A;i,j}$ analytically from the $Q$-function normalization/conventions; only after removing this factor is the result pairing-independent and equal to $\\Psi_L^A\\!\\cdot\\!\\Psi_R^A$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. Superseded diagnostic: per-ladder vacuum-normalized determinant\n\n> **Not the target norm construction.** This section is retained only to document the earlier diagnostic. Its two matrix rows were assigned to different inhomogeneity ladders. Section 8 replaces it by the requested construction in which both rows use the same full contour and differ only by their Q-function choices.\n\nFor this superseded per-ladder object we used\n\n$$\n\\widehat N_A^{(i,j)}=\n\\frac{N^{AA}_{i,j}}{N^{{\\rm vac},{\\rm vac}}_{i,j}},\n$$\n\nwith no division by $D_{00}$. The selected pairing was $(i,j)=(3,3)$, namely direct $q_3$ and dual $q^3$, for the complete $(S,P)=(1,1)$ multiplet. The formulas below use\n\n$$\n\\sigma=\\theta_1+\\theta_2,\\qquad \\delta=\\theta_1-\\theta_2.\n$$",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 17. Fully analytic Baxter solve and vacuum-normalized norms for (S,P)=(1,1). ---- *)\nClearAll[\n  UntwSolveAnalytic, analyticStates11, E2Analytic, LsumAnalytic,\n  N2dAnalytic, NAAAnalytic, analyticRatios11, analyticCenteredRatios11,\n  analyticBenchmarkCheck11\n  ];\n\nUntwSolveAnalytic[S_, P_, μ_] := Module[\n  {dh = Mdeg[S, P, μ] + Range[0, 3],\n   dd = μ[[{4, 3, 2, 1}]] + Range[0, 3], js = {4, 3, 2, 1},\n   x, pf, G, eqs, sol, rec, qd = <||>},\n  pf[k_] := Function[y,\n    Evaluate[y^dh[[k]] + Sum[cq[k, m] y^m, {m, 0, dh[[k]] - 1}]]];\n  eqs = Join[\n    DeleteCases[\n     Flatten@Table[\n       CoefficientList[Expand[BaxRes[S, P, μ][pf[k]][x]], x], {k, 4}], 0],\n    Flatten@Table[\n      If[dh[[l]] < dh[[k]], cq[k, dh[[l]]], Nothing],\n      {k, 4}, {l, k - 1}]];\n  sol = Solve[(# == 0 &) /@ eqs,\n    Join[tcvars,\n     Flatten@Table[cq[k, m], {k, 4}, {m, 0, dh[[k]] - 1}]]];\n  If[Length[sol] =!= 1, Return[$Failed]];\n  rec = <|\n    \"mu\" -> μ,\n    \"tc\" -> (tcvars /. First[sol]),\n    \"q\" -> Table[CoefficientList[pf[k][x] /. First[sol], x], {k, 4}]\n    |>;\n  Do[\n   With[{j = js[[a]]},\n    G = Function[y,\n      Evaluate[y^dd[[a]] + Sum[ce[j, m] y^m, {m, 0, dd[[a]] - 1}]]];\n    eqs = Join[\n      DeleteCases[\n       CoefficientList[\n        Expand[BaxResD[S, P, μ][G][x] /.\n          Thread[tcvars -> rec[\"tc\"]]], x], 0],\n      Table[If[dd[[b]] < dd[[a]], ce[j, dd[[b]]], Nothing],\n       {b, a - 1}]];\n    sol = Solve[(# == 0 &) /@ eqs,\n      Table[ce[j, m], {m, 0, dd[[a]] - 1}]];\n    qd[j] = If[Length[sol] === 1,\n      CoefficientList[G[x] /. First[sol], x], $Failed]],\n   {a, 4}];\n  Append[rec, \"qd\" -> qd]\n  ];\n\nanalyticStates11 = UntwSolveAnalytic[1, 1, #] & /@ irrepsSP[1, 1];\n\nE2Analytic[S_, P_][x_] :=\n  mMeas[S, P][x]/(ν1[S, P][x] ν1[S, P][x - h]);\n\nLsumAnalytic[S_, P_][f_, s_, x_] :=\n  Sum[Residue[\n    E2Analytic[S, P][x] f,\n    {x, {θ1, θ2}[[s]] + k h}],\n   {k, 0, {S, P}[[s]] + 1}];\n\nN2dAnalytic[S_, P_, A_, B_, i_, j_] := Module[\n  {x, qa, qb, g, f1, f2},\n  qa = Function[w, qpoly[A[\"qd\"][j], w]];\n  qb = Function[w, qpoly[B[\"q\"][[i]], w]];\n  g[y_] := qb[y] - qb[y - h];\n  f1 = Expand[qa[x] (\n      -ν1[S, P][x - h] g[x] + ν4[S, P][x] g[x - h])];\n  f2 = Expand[qa[x] qb[x - h]];\n  Table[{\n    LsumAnalytic[S, P][f1, s, x],\n    LsumAnalytic[S, P][f2, s, x]}, {s, 2}]\n  ];\n\nNAAAnalytic[S_, P_, state_, i_: 3, j_: 3] :=\n  Factor@Together@Det@N2dAnalytic[S, P, state, state, i, j];\n\nanalyticRatios11 = With[\n  {vac = First[analyticStates11]},\n  Table[Factor@Together[\n    NAAAnalytic[1, 1, state, 3, 3]/NAAAnalytic[1, 1, vac, 3, 3]],\n   {state, analyticStates11}]\n  ];\n\nanalyticCenteredRatios11 =\n  Factor@Together[# /. {\n       θ1 -> (σ + δ)/2, θ2 -> (σ - δ)/2}] & /@ analyticRatios11;\n\nanalyticBenchmarkCheck11 = MapThread[\n  Function[{state, formula},\n   With[{\n     benchmarkState = First@Select[states[1, 1],\n        Function[s, s[\"mu\"] === state[\"mu\"]]],\n     specialized = Together[formula /. {\n         σ -> ((θ1 + θ2) /. prm),\n         δ -> ((θ1 - θ2) /. prm), h -> (h /. prm)}]},\n    With[{existing = Nnormalized[1, 1, benchmarkState, 3, 3]},\n     {state[\"mu\"], specialized, existing,\n      Together[specialized - existing] === 0}]\n    ]],\n  {analyticStates11, analyticCenteredRatios11}];\n\nGrid[{\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[\n     MapThread[{#1[\"mu\"], #2} &,\n      {analyticStates11, analyticCenteredRatios11}],\n     {\"mu\", \"analytic NAA/Nvac for (i,j)=(3,3)\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]},\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[analyticBenchmarkCheck11,\n     {\"mu\", \"analytic formula at benchmark\", \"existing benchmark\",\n      \"exact match\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}\n  }, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"331408\" data-output-id=\"73\" data-out-n=\"559\" data-sub-idx=\"11\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"37\" data-sub-start=\"100\" data-sub-end=\"112\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[559]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"10\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:10.9502em;vertical-align:-5.2251em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.7251em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.7251em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.32em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.32em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.28em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.28em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:6.06em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.78em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.28em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.75em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.31em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">mu</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.55em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.31em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><s