an></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1748</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.1551em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:4.8102em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.1551em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.6551em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.8151em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">exact match</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.6151em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.2049em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.1551em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:4.8102em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.1551em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.6551em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7051em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.6551em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9102em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.6551em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1102em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.6551em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.3102em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.6551em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.1551em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.2251em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[559]= \\begin{array}{c}\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{mu} & \\text{analytic NAA/Nvac for (i,j)=(3,3)}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2,0,0\\right\\} & 1\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1,1,0\\right\\} & -\\frac{\\sigma \\,\\left(\\delta -\\sigma \\right)\\,\\left(\\delta +\\sigma \\right)\\,\\left(\\delta ^2+8\\,h^2+12\\,h\\,\\sigma +3\\,\\sigma ^2\\right)}{\\left(2\\,h+\\sigma \\right)\\,\\left(3\\,\\delta ^4-6\\,\\delta ^2\\,\\sigma ^2-12\\,\\delta ^2\\,h^2-4\\,h^2\\,\\sigma ^2+3\\,\\sigma ^4\\right)}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1,1,1\\right\\} & -\\frac{\\left(2\\,h-\\delta \\right)\\,\\left(\\delta +2\\,h\\right)\\,\\left(-3\\,\\delta ^2+4\\,h^2+3\\,\\sigma ^2\\right)}{3\\,\\left(-3\\,\\delta ^4+6\\,\\delta ^2\\,\\sigma ^2+12\\,\\delta ^2\\,h^2+4\\,h^2\\,\\sigma ^2-3\\,\\sigma ^4\\right)}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}\\\\\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{mu} & \\text{analytic formula at benchmark} & \\text{existing benchmark} & \\text{exact match}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2,0,0\\right\\} & 1 & 1 & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1,1,0\\right\\} & -\\frac{7955}{18564} & -\\frac{7955}{18564} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1,1,1\\right\\} & -\\frac{1748}{357} & -\\frac{1748}{357} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "760de0fa-4a5a-4d13-a475-838ba11a92dd"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "> **Superseded per-ladder result.** The inhomogeneity dependence below is not evidence for the requested full-contour norm; it disappears after both determinant rows are summed over the same complete residue set in Section 8.\n\nDefine the common denominator\n\n$$\n\\mathcal D=3\\delta^4-6\\delta^2\\sigma^2-12h^2\\delta^2-4h^2\\sigma^2+3\\sigma^4.\n$$\n\nThe three per-ladder diagnostic results are\n\n$$\n\\widehat N_{[2,2,0,0]}=1,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\widehat N_{[2,1,1,0]}\n=-\\frac{\\sigma(\\delta^2-\\sigma^2)\n (\\delta^2+8h^2+12h\\sigma+3\\sigma^2)}\n {(2h+\\sigma)\\mathcal D},\n$$\n\n$$\n\\widehat N_{[1,1,1,1]}\n=\\frac{(4h^2-\\delta^2)(4h^2-3\\delta^2+3\\sigma^2)}\n {3\\mathcal D}.\n$$\n\nAt $\\theta_1=1/3$, $\\theta_2=1/7$, $h=1$, these give $1,-7955/18564,-1748/357$. They remain useful as an exact check of the residue code, but they are not used as the norm from Section 8 onward.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 7. Analytic audit of the transfer-matrix left/right norm\n\nThe earlier transfer-matrix calculation fixed $\\theta_1=1/3$, $\\theta_2=1/7$, and $h=1$. Here we repeat it with all three parameters symbolic. The Lax matrix is\n\n$$\nL_\\lambda(u-\\theta_s)_{ij}\n=(u-\\theta_s)\\delta_{ij}\\mathbf 1-hJ_{ji}^{(s)},\n$$\n\nand every quantum-minor shift is also changed from one unit to $h$. We use the analytic Baxter eigenvalues from the preceding section, restrict to each highest-weight sector, normalize the first nonzero component of each right and transpose-left eigenvector to one, and check both $\\tau_1$ and $\\tau_2$ exactly.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 18. Symbolic-theta,h audit of PsiL.PsiR for the (S,P)=(1,1) multiplet. ---- *)\nClearAll[\n  hnLaxAnalytic, hnTmonoAnalytic, hnTgAnalytic,\n  hnQminVAnalytic, hnTauVAnalytic, honestOneAnalytic,\n  honestAnalytic11, honestAnalyticNumericalAgreement11\n  ];\n\nhnLaxAnalytic[lam_, x_] := Table[\n  SparseArray[\n   x KroneckerDelta[i, j] IdentityMatrix[hnDim[lam]]\n    - h hnJJ[j, i, lam]],\n  {i, 4}, {j, 4}];\n\nhnTmonoAnalytic[sites_, x_] := Fold[\n  Function[{mon, site},\n   With[{lx = hnLaxAnalytic[site[[1]], x - site[[2]]]},\n    Table[\n     Sum[KroneckerProduct[mon[[i, k]], lx[[k, j]]], {k, 4}],\n     {i, 4}, {j, 4}]]],\n  hnLaxAnalytic[sites[[1, 1]], x - sites[[1, 2]]],\n  Rest[sites]];\n\nhnTgAnalytic[sites_, zs_, x_][i_, j_] :=\n  zs[[i]] hnTmonoAnalytic[sites, x][[i, j]];\n\nhnQminVAnalytic[sites_, zs_, inds_List, x_, vec_] := Sum[\n  Module[{res = vec},\n   Do[\n    res = hnTgAnalytic[sites, zs, x - (k - 1) h][\n       inds[[perm[[k]]]], inds[[k]]] . res,\n    {k, Length[inds], 1, -1}];\n   Signature[perm] res],\n  {perm, Permutations[Range[Length[inds]]]}];\n\nhnTauVAnalytic[sites_, zs_, a_, x_, vec_] :=\n  Sum[hnQminVAnalytic[sites, zs, inds, x, vec],\n   {inds, Subsets[Range[4], {a}]}];\n\nModule[\n {reps = {{1, 1, 0, 0}, {1, 1, 0, 0}}, sites, dims,\n  totalDim, localWeights1, localWeights2, totalWeights, id, t1, t2},\n sites = {{reps[[1]], θ1}, {reps[[2]], θ2}};\n dims = hnDim /@ reps;\n totalDim = Times @@ dims;\n localWeights1 =\n  (Table[hnJ0[k][#], {k, 4}] &) /@ hnPs[{reps[[1]]}];\n localWeights2 =\n  (Table[hnJ0[k][#], {k, 4}] &) /@ hnPs[{reps[[2]]}];\n totalWeights = Flatten[\n   Table[localWeights1[[ii]] + localWeights2[[jj]],\n    {ii, dims[[1]]}, {jj, dims[[2]]}], 1];\n id = IdentityMatrix[totalDim, SparseArray];\n t1 = hnTauVAnalytic[sites, ConstantArray[1, 4], 1, 0, id];\n t2 = hnTauVAnalytic[sites, ConstantArray[1, 4], 2, 0, id];\n\n honestOneAnalytic[state_] := Module[\n   {mu = state[\"mu\"], lambda1 = state[\"tc\"][[1]],\n    lambda2 = state[\"tc\"][[4]], sector, block1, block2,\n    nullR, nullL, psiR, psiL, norm},\n   sector = Flatten@Position[totalWeights, mu];\n   block1 = t1[[sector, sector]];\n   block2 = t2[[sector, sector]];\n   nullR = NullSpace[\n     block1 - lambda1 IdentityMatrix[Length[sector]]];\n   nullL = NullSpace[\n     Transpose[block1] - lambda1 IdentityMatrix[Length[sector]]];\n   psiR = hnPivotNormalize@First[nullR];\n   psiL = hnPivotNormalize@First[nullL];\n   norm = Factor@Together[psiL . psiR];\n   <|\n    \"mu\" -> mu, \"sector\" -> sector,\n    \"PsiRsector\" -> psiR, \"PsiLsector\" -> psiL,\n    \"honestNorm\" -> norm,\n    \"parameterIndependent\" -> FreeQ[{psiR, psiL, norm}, θ1 | θ2 | h],\n    \"tau1Right\" ->\n     (Simplify[block1 . psiR - lambda1 psiR] ===\n       ConstantArray[0, Length[sector]]),\n    \"tau1Left\" ->\n     (Simplify[Transpose[block1] . psiL - lambda1 psiL] ===\n       ConstantArray[0, Length[sector]]),\n    \"tau2Right\" ->\n     (Simplify[block2 . psiR - lambda2 psiR] ===\n       ConstantArray[0, Length[sector]]),\n    \"tau2Left\" ->\n     (Simplify[Transpose[block2] . psiL - lambda2 psiL] ===\n       ConstantArray[0, Length[sector]])\n    |>\n   ];\n honestAnalytic11 = honestOneAnalytic /@ analyticStates11;\n ];\n\nhonestAnalyticNumericalAgreement11 = Map[\n  Function[row,\n   With[{old = honestDatum[1, 1, row[\"mu\"]], sector = row[\"sector\"]},\n    {row[\"mu\"],\n     Together[Normal[old[\"PsiR\"]][[sector]] - row[\"PsiRsector\"]] ===\n      ConstantArray[0, Length[sector]],\n     Together[Normal[old[\"PsiL\"]][[sector]] - row[\"PsiLsector\"]] ===\n      ConstantArray[0, Length[sector]],\n     old[\"honestNorm\"] === row[\"honestNorm\"]}\n    ]], honestAnalytic11];\n\nGrid[{\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[\n     ({#[\"mu\"], #[\"PsiRsector\"], #[\"PsiLsector\"],\n        #[\"honestNorm\"], #[\"parameterIndependent\"],\n        And[#[\"tau1Right\"], #[\"tau1Left\"],\n         #[\"tau2Right\"], #[\"tau2Left\"]]} &) /@ honestAnalytic11,\n     {\"mu\", \"PsiR in HW sector\", \"PsiL in HW sector\",\n      \"PsiL.PsiR\", \"independent of theta1,theta2,h\",\n      \"tau1/tau2 right/left checks\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]},\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[honestAnalyticNumericalAgreement11,\n     {\"mu\", \"PsiR matches old benchmark\", \"PsiL matches old benchmark\",\n      \"norm matches old benchmark\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}\n  }, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"331408\" data-output-id=\"74\" data-out-n=\"568\" data-sub-idx=\"9\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"40\" data-sub-start=\"102\" data-sub-end=\"118\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[568]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"18\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:9.69em;vertical-align:-4.595em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.095em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.095em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.695em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.695em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.655em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:4.81em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.155em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.655em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.815em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">mu</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.615em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span c