\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">PsiL.PsiR</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.6151em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.2049em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">6</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.1551em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:4.8102em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.1551em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.6551em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.8151em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">constant conversion to honest norm</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.6151em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">3</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">4</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.2049em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">12</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.1551em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:4.8102em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.1551em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.6551em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7051em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.6551em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9102em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.6551em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1102em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.6551em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.3102em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.6551em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.1551em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.5951em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[581]= \\begin{array}{c}\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{mu} & \\text{HW nullity} & \\text{tau1..tau3 eigenchecks} & \\text{4 direct + 4 dual solution counts} & \\text{direct Q agrees} & \\text{dual Q agrees}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2,0,0\\right\\} & 1 & \\left\\{\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True}\\right\\} & \\left\\{1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1\\right\\} & \\mathrm{True} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1,1,0\\right\\} & 1 & \\left\\{\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True}\\right\\} & \\left\\{1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1\\right\\} & \\mathrm{True} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1,1,1\\right\\} & 1 & \\left\\{\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True}\\right\\} & \\left\\{1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1\\right\\} & \\mathrm{True} & \\mathrm{True}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}\\\\\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{mu} & \\text{full-contour NAA/Nvac} & \\text{independent of theta1,theta2,h} & \\text{PsiL.PsiR} & \\text{constant conversion to honest norm}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,2,0,0\\right\\} & 1 & \\mathrm{True} & 1 & 1\\\\\\hline\\left\\{2,1,1,0\\right\\} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\mathrm{True} & 2 & \\frac{4}{3}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{1,1,1,1\\right\\} & \\frac{1}{2} & \\mathrm{True} & 6 & 12\\\\\\hline\\end{array}\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "b041406a-ce36-499e-b852-b48ba6facc40"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "The corrected full-contour result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\widetilde N_A}{\\widetilde N_{\\rm vac}}\n=1,\\quad \\frac32,\\quad \\frac12\n$$\n\nfor $\\mu=[2,2,0,0],[2,1,1,0],[1,1,1,1]$, respectively. All three values are exactly independent of $\\theta_1,\\theta_2,h$. Therefore the inhomogeneity dependence found in the superseded per-ladder determinant does not require cancellation by special-point Q-products: it was caused by using the wrong row construction.\n\nThe remaining discrepancy with the pivot-gauge biorthogonal norms $1,2,6$ is parameter-independent:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\Psi_L\\cdot\\Psi_R}\n {\\widetilde N_A/\\widetilde N_{\\rm vac}}\n=1,\\quad \\frac43,\\quad 12.\n$$\n\nA Q-normalization formula may still explain these state-dependent constants, but it is no longer needed to remove any inhomogeneity dependence. Such a formula should be tested only after fixing this full-contour row convention.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 9. More representations: the full-contour norm is a universal combinatorial factor\n\nKeep the corrected convention from Section 8: both determinant rows use the same full set of residues, and the rows differ only by the Q-pairing. We use the row pair \\`{{3,3},{4,4}}\\` and divide only by the vacuum determinant for the same $(S,P)$.\n\nWrite\n$$\nL=S+P,\\qquad \\mu=(L-j,L-k,k,j),\\qquad 0\\leq j\\leq k\\leq \\min(S,P).\n$$\nThe exact data below extend the comparison from the original 12 states to\n$$\n(S,P)=(1,1),(2,1),(2,2),(3,1),(3,2),(4,1),(4,2),(3,3),(4,3).\n$$\nFor all 50 states the vacuum-normalized SoV determinant is\n$$\n\\boxed{\\displaystyle\n{\\cal N}_{\\rm SoV}(L;j,k)\n=\\frac{N^{AA}_{\\mu}}{N^{AA}_{\\rm vac}}\n=\\frac{(k-j+1)(L+2-j-k)}{L+2}.}\n$$\nThis is an exact verification on the displayed finite family, not yet an all-spin proof. In particular, it is independent of $\\theta_1,\\theta_2,\\hbar$, and even of the split $L=S+P$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 9. Extended representations and the corrected SoV/Hilbert relation. ---- *)\nClearAll[\n  extendedSPPairs, honestNormDataExtended, fullContourDetCorrect,\n  fullContourVacDetCorrect, fullContourSoVRatioCorrect,\n  fullContourSoVClosed, extendedNormRelationData, dimSS,\n  hilbertJ0Closed, hilbert11Closed\n  ];\n\nextendedSPPairs = {{1, 1}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}, {3, 1}, {3, 2},\n   {4, 1}, {4, 2}, {3, 3}, {4, 3}};\n\nhonestNormDataExtended =\n  Flatten[Map[honestStateData @@ # &, extendedSPPairs], 1];\n\nfullContourDetCorrect[S_, P_, state_] := Together@Det[{\n    rowFull[S, P, state, state, 3, 3],\n    rowFull[S, P, state, state, 4, 4]\n    }];\n\nfullContourVacDetCorrect[S_, P_] :=\n  fullContourVacDetCorrect[S, P] =\n   fullContourDetCorrect[S, P, vacuumState[S, P]];\n\nfullContourSoVRatioCorrect[S_, P_, state_] := Together[\n   fullContourDetCorrect[S, P, state]/\n    fullContourVacDetCorrect[S, P]\n   ];\n\nfullContourSoVClosed[L_, j_, k_] :=\n  (k - j + 1) (L + 2 - j - k)/(L + 2);\n\nextendedNormRelationData = Flatten[\n   Map[\n    Function[sp,\n     Module[{ss = sp[[1]], pp = sp[[2]], ll = Total[sp]},\n      Map[\n       Function[state,\n        Module[{mu = state[\"mu\"], j, k, sov, hilbert, closed},\n         j = mu[[4]];\n         k = mu[[3]];\n         sov = fullContourSoVRatioCorrect[ss, pp, state];\n         hilbert = (First@Select[\n             honestNormDataExtended,\n             Function[row,\n              row[\"SP\"] === sp && row[\"mu\"] === mu]\n             ])[\"honestNorm\"];\n         closed = fullContourSoVClosed[ll, j, k];\n         <|\"SP\" -> sp, \"mu\" -> mu, \"j\" -> j, \"k\" -> k,\n          \"SoVRatio\" -> sov, \"SoVClosed\" -> closed,\n          \"HilbertNorm\" -> hilbert,\n          \"HilbertOverSoV\" -> Together[hilbert/sov],\n          \"SoVFormulaCheck\" -> Together[sov - closed] === 0|>\n         ]],\n       states[ss, pp]]\n      ]],\n    extendedSPPairs],\n   1];\n\ndimSS[n_] := (n + 1) (n + 2)^2 (n + 3)/12;\nhilbertJ0Closed[S_, P_, k_] :=\n  Binomial[S + P - k + 1, k]/Binomial[S, k];\nhilbert11Closed[S_, P_] :=\n  Binomial[S + P + 2, 2]/Binomial[S + 1, 2];\n\nGrid[{\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[\n     ({#[\"SP\"], #[\"mu\"], #[\"j\"], #[\"k\"], #[\"SoVRatio\"],\n         #[\"HilbertNorm\"], #[\"HilbertOverSoV\"]} &) /@\n      extendedNormRelationData,\n     {\"(S,P)\", \"mu\", \"j\", \"k\", \"NAA/Nvac\",\n      \"PsiL.PsiR\", \"(PsiL.PsiR)/(NAA/Nvac)\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]},\n  {Grid[{\n     {\"exact SoV formula for every displayed state\",\n      And @@ extendedNormRelationData[[All, \"SoVFormulaCheck\"]]},\n     {\"number of exact states\", Length[extendedNormRelationData]},\n     {\"j=0 Hilbert subfamily\",\n      And @@ Map[\n        Function[row,\n         If[row[\"j\"] === 0,\n          Together[row[\"HilbertNorm\"] -\n             hilbertJ0Closed[\n              row[\"SP\"][[1]], row[\"SP\"][[2]], row[\"k\"]]] === 0,\n          True]],\n        extendedNormRelationData]},\n     {\"j=k=1 Hilbert subfamily\",\n      And @@ Map[\n        Function[row,\n         If[row[\"j\"] === 1 && row[\"k\"] === 1,\n          Together[row[\"HilbertNorm\"] -\n             hilbert11Closed[\n              row[\"SP\"][[1]], row[\"SP\"][[2]]]] === 0,\n          True]],\n        extendedNormRelationData]},\n     {\"maximally contracted edge j=k=P\",\n      And @@ Map[\n        Function[row,\n         If[row[\"j\"] === row[\"SP\"][[2]] &&\n            row[\"k\"] === row[\"SP\"][[2]],\n          Together[row[\"HilbertNorm\"] -\n             dimSS[row[\"SP\"][[1]]]/\n              dimSS[row[\"SP\"][[1]] - row[\"SP\"][[2]]]] === 0,\n          True]],\n        extendedNormRelationData]}\n     }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}\n  }, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<details class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer\">4 warnings</summary><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Det::matsq: Argument {rowFull[1, 1, &lt;|mu -&gt; {2, 2, 0, 0}, tc -&gt; {--, ----, -(----), ----, ---}, q -&gt; {{1}, {0, 1}, {0, 0, -(-), -(--), 1}, {0, 0, ---, -(----), 0, 1}}, qd -&gt; &lt;|4 -&gt; {1}, 3 -&gt; {0, 1}, 2 -&gt; {0, 0, --, -(---), 1}, 1 -&gt; {0, 0, -----, -(-----), 0, 1}|&gt;|&gt;, &lt;|mu -&gt; {2, 2, 0, 0}, tc -&gt; {--, ----, -(----), ----, ---}, q -&gt; {{1}, {0, 1}, {0, 0, -(-), -(--), 1}, {0, 0, ---, -(----), 0, 1}}, qd -&gt; &lt;|4 -&gt; {1}, 3 -&gt; {0, 1}, 2 -&gt; {0, 0, --, -(---), 1}, 1 -&gt; {0, 0, -----, -(-----), 0, 1}|&gt;|&gt;, 3, 3], rowFull[1, 1, &lt;|mu -&gt; {2, 2, 0, 0}, tc -&gt; {--, ----, -(----), ----, ---}, q -&gt; {{1}, {0, 1}, {0, 0, -(-), -(--), 1}, {0, 0, ---, -(----), 0, 1}}, qd -&gt; &lt;|4 -&gt; {1}, 3 -&gt; {0, 1}, 2 -&gt; {0, 0, --, -(---), 1}, 1 -&gt; {0, 0, -----, -(-----), 0, 1}|&gt;|&gt;, &lt;|mu -&gt; {2, 2, 0, 0}, tc -&gt; {--, ----, -(----), ----, ---}, q -&gt; {{1}, {0, 1}, {0, 0, -(-), -(--), 1}, {0, 0, ---, -(----), 0, 1}}, qd -&gt; &lt;|4 -&gt; {1}, 3 -&gt; {0, 1}, 2 -&gt; {0, 0, --, -(---), 1}, 1 -&gt; {0, 0, -----, -(-----), 0, 1}|&gt;|&gt;, 4, 4]} at position 1 is not a non-empty square matrix.                                                                  7   147     147    441   21                                7     21              441    1323                                                      7     21                     441     1323                                            7   147     147    441   21                                7     21              441    1323                                                      7     