  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "The corrected relation in the present monic-Q / pivot-eigenvector gauges is therefore\n$$\n\\boxed{\\displaystyle\n\\Psi_L\\!\\cdot\\!\\Psi_R\n=F_{S,P;j,k}\\,\n\\frac{(k-j+1)(L+2-j-k)}{L+2},\n\\qquad\nF_{S,P;j,k}:=\n\\frac{\\Psi_L\\!\\cdot\\!\\Psi_R}{N^{AA}_{\\mu}/N^{AA}_{\\rm vac}}.}\n$$\nThe table evaluates $F$ exactly. The SoV part is already a simple universal combinatorial factor. The remaining $F$ is representation-normalization data: it depends on the split $(S,P)$, as a Hilbert-space Clebsch--Gordan normalization should.\n\nThree nontrivial Hilbert subfamilies already collapse to elementary combinatorics:\n$$\n\\left.\\Psi_L\\!\\cdot\\!\\Psi_R\\right|_{j=0}\n =\\frac{\\binom{L-k+1}{k}}{\\binom{S}{k}},\n\\qquad\n\\left.\\Psi_L\\!\\cdot\\!\\Psi_R\\right|_{j=k=1}\n =\\frac{\\binom{L+2}{2}}{\\binom{S+1}{2}},\n$$\nand on the maximally contracted edge $j=k=P$,\n$$\n\\Psi_L\\!\\cdot\\!\\Psi_R\n=\\frac{\\dim[S,S]}{\\dim[S-P,S-P]},\n\\qquad\n\\dim[n,n]=\\frac{(n+1)(n+2)^2(n+3)}{12}.\n$$\nAll three identities pass every applicable exact row in the enlarged table.\n\nBecause the corrected SoV result is already independent of the inhomogeneities, evaluations such as $Q(\\theta_\\alpha+\\text{shift})$ are not required to cancel $\\theta$-dependence. They may still provide a compact expression for the remaining eigenvector gauge factor $F_{S,P;j,k}$, but any such formula must reproduce the elementary binomial and dimension-ratio limits above. Interior families such as $j=1,k=2$ are the next discriminating test; fitting them prematurely to one Q-product would obscure the simpler combinatorial structure already established.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 10. Comparing Q choices and a special-point Q formula\n\nIn the corrected construction one determinant requires two full-contour rows.  It is therefore useful to write\n$$\n\\widehat N^{AA}_{r_1,r_2}\n=\n\\frac{\\det\\{\\mathcal R_{r_1},\\mathcal R_{r_2}\\}_A}\n     {\\det\\{\\mathcal R_{r_1},\\mathcal R_{r_2}\\}_{\\rm vac}},\n\\qquad r=(i,j)\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\ (q_i,q^j).\n$$\nAmong diagonal rows $r=(a,a)$, the four universally nonzero determinant choices are\n$$\n(1,2),\\quad(1,3),\\quad(2,4),\\quad(3,4),\n$$\nwhere $(a,b)$ abbreviates the row pair $\\{(a,a),(b,b)\\}$.\n\nAll four give the same vacuum-normalized norm on every one of the 50 states:\n$$\n\\boxed{\\displaystyle\n\\frac{\\widehat N^{AA}_{a,b}}{\\widehat N^{AA}_{a',b'}}=1\n\\quad\\text{for the four admissible diagonal choices}.}\n$$\nEquivalently, before vacuum normalization their determinant ratio is state independent and equals the same ratio evaluated on the vacuum.  This means that changing between these diagonal Q choices cannot remove the Hilbert/SoV conversion factor: that factor is common to all four.\n\nGeneric mixed rows are different.  The 41 universally nonzero row pairs produce many distinct normalized values on non-vacuum states, so the diagonal equality is a Q-system identity rather than arbitrary pairing independence.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 10. Q-pairing ratios and the hook-normalized special Q12 value. ---- *)\nClearAll[\n  diagonalFullPairs, fullPairDet, fullPairNhat,\n  diagonalPairComparison, diagonalPairSummary,\n  monicQ12, q12Degree, q12Top1Single,\n  q12Top1ShiftedSingle, q12Top1Hook,\n  q12NormRows, q12HookChecks, qPairCandidateLedger\n  ];\n\ndiagonalFullPairs = {\n   {{1, 1}, {2, 2}}, {{1, 1}, {3, 3}},\n   {{2, 2}, {4, 4}}, {{3, 3}, {4, 4}}\n   };\n\nfullPairDet[S_, P_, state_, pair_] := Together@Det[\n   Map[\n    Function[ij,\n     rowFull[S, P, state, state, ij[[1]], ij[[2]]]],\n    pair]\n   ];\n\nfullPairNhat[S_, P_, state_, pair_] := Together[\n   fullPairDet[S, P, state, pair]/\n    fullPairDet[S, P, vacuumState[S, P], pair]\n   ];\n\ndiagonalPairComparison = Flatten[\n   Map[\n    Function[sp,\n     Map[\n      Function[state,\n       Module[{vals =\n          Map[fullPairNhat[sp[[1]], sp[[2]], state, #] &,\n           diagonalFullPairs]},\n        <|\"SP\" -> sp, \"mu\" -> state[\"mu\"], \"values\" -> vals,\n         \"allEqual\" -> SameQ @@ vals|>\n        ]],\n      states @@ sp]],\n    extendedSPPairs],\n   1];\n\ndiagonalPairSummary = Map[\n   Function[sp,\n    Module[{rows =\n       Select[diagonalPairComparison, #[\"SP\"] === sp &]},\n     {sp, Length[rows], And @@ rows[[All, \"allEqual\"]]}\n     ]],\n   extendedSPPairs];\n\nmonicQ12[state_][z_] := Module[{y, w, lc, hh = h /. prm},\n   w = Expand[\n     qpoly[state[\"q\"][[1]], y] qpoly[state[\"q\"][[2]], y - hh] -\n      qpoly[state[\"q\"][[1]], y - hh] qpoly[state[\"q\"][[2]], y]\n     ];\n   lc = Coefficient[w, y, Exponent[w, y]];\n   Expand[(w/lc) /. y -> z]\n   ];\n\nq12Degree[state_] := Module[{y},\n   Exponent[monicQ12[state][y], y]\n   ];\n\nq12Top1Single[S_, P_, state_] := Module[\n   {d = q12Degree[state], hh = h /. prm,\n    t = ((θ1 - θ2)/h) /. prm, endpoint},\n   endpoint = (θ1 + S h) /. prm;\n   Together[\n    monicQ12[state][endpoint]/\n     (hh^d If[d === 0, 1,\n       Product[S + t + a, {a, 0, d - 1}]])\n    ]\n   ];\n\nq12Top1ShiftedSingle[S_, P_, state_] := Module[\n   {j = state[\"mu\"][[4]], k = state[\"mu\"][[3]],\n    d = q12Degree[state], hh = h /. prm,\n    t = ((θ1 - θ2)/h) /. prm, endpoint},\n   endpoint = (θ1 + S h) /. prm;\n   Together[\n    monicQ12[state][endpoint]/\n     (hh^d If[d === 0, 1,\n       Product[S - k + 1 + t + a, {a, 0, d - 1}]])\n    ]\n   ];\n\nq12Top1Hook[S_, P_, state_] := Module[\n   {j = state[\"mu\"][[4]], k = state[\"mu\"][[3]],\n    hh = h /. prm, t = ((θ1 - θ2)/h) /. prm, endpoint},\n   endpoint = (θ1 + S h) /. prm;\n   Together[\n    monicQ12[state][endpoint]/\n     (hh^(j + k)\n       If[k === 0, 1,\n        Product[S - k + 1 + t + a, {a, 0, k - 1}]]\n       If[j === 0, 1,\n        Product[S - j + 2 + t + a, {a, 0, j - 1}]])\n    ]\n   ];\n\nq12NormRows = Map[\n   Function[row,\n    Module[{sp = row[\"SP\"], state, qhook},\n     state = First@Select[\n        states @@ sp, #[\"mu\"] === row[\"mu\"] &];\n     qhook = q12Top1Hook[sp[[1]], sp[[2]], state];\n     {sp, row[\"mu\"], row[\"j\"], row[\"k\"],\n      row[\"HilbertNorm\"], qhook,\n      Together[row[\"HilbertNorm\"] qhook],\n      Together[1/(row[\"SoVRatio\"] qhook)]}\n     ]],\n   extendedNormRelationData];\n\nq12HookChecks = (#[[7]] === 1 &) /@ q12NormRows;\n\nqPairCandidateLedger = {\n   {\"four diagonal determinant choices\",\n    \"independently validated\",\n    \"50/50 exact states\", 0,\n    \"Their pairwise vacuum-normalized ratios are 1.\"},\n   {\"all 41 admissible mixed row pairs agree\",\n    \"numerically rejected\",\n    \"12 original benchmark states\",\n    \"24 or 27 distinct values on each non-vacuum state\",\n    \"Only the diagonal Q-system subfamily is pairing independent.\"},\n   {\"Q12 top / (h^d (S+t)_d)\",\n    \"numerically rejected\",\n    \"all 50 exact states\", 23,\n    \"Works for vacua and k=1 only.\"},\n   {\"Q12 top / (h^d (S-k+1+t)_d)\",\n    \"numerically rejected\",\n    \"all 50 exact states\", 9,\n    \"Works for j=0,1; fails at j>=2.\"},\n   {\"Q12 top / [h^(j+k) (S-k+1+t)_k (S-j+2+t)_j]\",\n    \"independently validated\",\n    \"50/50 exact states\", Count[q12HookChecks, False],\n    \"Its inverse is exactly PsiL.PsiR.\"}\n   };\n\nGrid[{\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[diagonalPairSummary,\n     {\"(S,P)\", \"number of states\",\n      \"all four diagonal Nhat values equal\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]},\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[\n     ({#[\"SP\"], #[\"mu\"], Sequence @@ #[\"values\"]} &) /@\n      Select[diagonalPairComparison, #[\"SP\"] === {1, 1} &],\n     {\"(S,P)\", \"mu\", \"Nhat12\", \"Nhat13\", \"Nhat24\", \"Nhat34\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]},\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[q12NormRows,\n     {\"(S,P)\", \"mu\", \"j\", \"k\", \"PsiL.PsiR\",\n      \"hook-normalized Q12(top1)\", \"product check\",\n      \"Hilbert/SoV from Q\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]},\n  {Grid[\n    Prepend[qPairCandidateLedger,\n     {\"candidate\", \"status\", \"evidence\", \"failures\",\n      \"conclusion\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}\n  }, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
