   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Define the monic Casoratian\n$$\n\\bar Q_{12}(u)=\n\\operatorname{monic}\\!\\left[\nq_1(u)q_2(u-\\hbar)-q_1(u-\\hbar)q_2(u)\n\\right],\n\\qquad \\deg\\bar Q_{12}=j+k,\n$$\nand set\n$$\nt=\\frac{\\theta_1-\\theta_2}{\\hbar}.\n$$\nThe correct special value is at the top of the first inhomogeneity ladder, while its kinematic normalization is the product of two content strings:\n$$\n\\widehat Q_{12}^{(1)}\n=\n\\frac{\\bar Q_{12}(\\theta_1+S\\hbar)}\n{\\hbar^{j+k}(S-k+1+t)_k(S-j+2+t)_j}.\n$$\nFor all 50 tested states,\n$$\n\\boxed{\\displaystyle\n\\Psi_L\\!\\cdot\\!\\Psi_R\n=\\frac{1}{\\widehat Q_{12}^{(1)}}\n=\n\\frac{\\hbar^{j+k}(S-k+1+t)_k(S-j+2+t)_j}\n{\\bar Q_{12}(\\theta_1+S\\hbar)}.}\n$$\nCombining this with the universal full-contour SoV norm gives\n$$\n\\boxed{\\displaystyle\n\\frac{\\Psi_L\\!\\cdot\\!\\Psi_R}\n     {N^{AA}_\\mu/N^{AA}_{\\rm vac}}\n=\n\\frac{L+2}\n{(k-j+1)(L+2-j-k)\\,\\widehat Q_{12}^{(1)}}.}\n$$\nEquivalently,\n$$\n\\frac{N^{AA}_\\mu/N^{AA}_{\\rm vac}}\n{\\Psi_L\\!\\cdot\\!\\Psi_R}\n=\n\\frac{(k-j+1)(L+2-j-k)}{L+2}\\,\n\\widehat Q_{12}^{(1)}.\n$$\n\nThe candidate ledger records two useful false starts.  Normalizing by one rising string $(S+t)_{j+k}$ works only through $k=1$.  Shifting that string to $(S-k+1+t)_{j+k}$ extends it through $j=1$, but fails at $j\\geq2$.  The successful normalization splits it into\n$$\n(S-k+1+t)_k\\,(S-j+2+t)_j,\n$$\nwhich gives the repeated content factors expected when the two excitation labels overlap.  The resulting identity is independently validated on all 50 exact states; an all-$(S,P;j,k)$ analytic proof remains open.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 11. Table of $\\widehat Q_{12}^{(1)}$ for the first representations\n\nThe following table lists every allowed state for\n$$\n(S,P)=(1,1),(2,1),(2,2),(3,1),(3,2).\n$$\nThe values are calculated directly from the hook-normalized special-point Casoratian in Section 10, rather than entered by hand.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 11. Compact exact table of hook-normalized Q12 values. ---- *)\nClearAll[firstQhatSP, firstQhatRows];\nfirstQhatSP = {{1, 1}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}, {3, 1}, {3, 2}};\nfirstQhatRows = Map[\n   Function[row,\n    {row[[1]], row[[2]], row[[3]], row[[4]], row[[6]],\n     Together[1/row[[5]]], row[[7]] === 1}],\n   Select[q12NormRows, MemberQ[firstQhatSP, #[[1]]] &]\n   ];\n\nGrid[\n Prepend[firstQhatRows,\n  {\"(S,P)\", \"mu\", \"j\", \"k\",\n   \"Qhat12^(1)\", \"1/(PsiL.PsiR)\", \"exact match\"}],\n Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"331408\" data-output-id=\"81\" data-out-n=\"649\" data-sub-idx=\"4\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"52\" data-sub-start=\"10\" data-sub-end=\"14\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[649]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"18\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:26.5217em;vertical-align:-12.9909em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:13.5309em;\"><span style=\"top:-15.4909em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:15.4909em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:26.4817em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-12.9909em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:13.4909em;\"><span style=\"top:-15.6509em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">(S,P)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-14.4509em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span s